{#
  ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  DISPLAY & READING, APPLIED BEFORE THE FIRST PAINT — REFERENCE §7.5, §10
  ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

  Inline and nonced, in <head>, before any stylesheet. A linked script is fetched and
  run AFTER the first paint, so somebody who asked for 150% text would watch the page
  draw at 100% and jump. This is a deliberate duplicate of `AGA11y.apply()` in
  `a11y.js`, kept to the few lines the job needs; `DisplayReadingTest` compares the two
  maps key by key, so they cannot drift apart silently.

  ── THE MEMBER'S SAVED SETTINGS COME FIRST ──────────────────────────────────

  `member_display()` is the signed-in member's saved settings
  (Services\DisplayReadingPrefs), written into this script by the server — so a device
  the member has never used paints in their settings with nothing fetched. When there
  are none (signed out, or never saved) it is `null` and this browser's own store
  decides. The member's copy is also written back into the store, so `a11y.js` and every
  control read one answer from then on.

  ── THE EASY-READ FONT IS LOADED HERE, AND ONLY WHEN IT IS ON ───────────────

  `ag-easy` used to switch the body to Atkinson Hyperlegible, which nothing loaded — so
  the browser silently fell back to the face it already had and the setting changed the
  letter spacing and nothing else (GAPS §2). The face is fetched only for somebody who
  asked for it: a stylesheet everybody downloads for a setting few turn on is weight on
  every page. The address is the layout's `data-ag-easy-font`, the one place it is
  written; `a11y.js` reads the same attribute when the switch is turned on later.

  ── WHICH STORE IS THE VISITOR'S PREFERENCES ANSWER (`data-ag-keep`) ───────

  Kept between visits (`localStorage`) only when they allowed Preferences; otherwise for
  this tab (`sessionStorage`), so the settings still work and are forgotten when it
  closes — CookiePrefs decides, the layout hands the answer over as `data-ag-keep`. A copy
  in the store the answer does not allow is MOVED, so saying no actually takes the
  settings off the device and saying yes keeps what was set this visit. Both calls are
  spelled out rather than held in a variable, so the storage sweep (CookieRegistryTest)
  can see every write.

  The language is NOT here: it is a cookie, already on <html lang dir> in the markup the
  server sent. Wrapped throughout, because `localStorage` THROWS in a Safari private
  window, and a settings script that takes the page down is worse than one that forgets.
#}
<script nonce="{{ csp_nonce }}">
(function(){var d=document.documentElement,c=d.classList,m={{ member_display()|json_encode(JSON_SAFE)|raw }},s={},K=d.getAttribute('data-ag-keep')==='1',v=null;
try{if(K){v=sessionStorage.getItem('ag-a11y');if(v!==null&&localStorage.getItem('ag-a11y')===null)localStorage.setItem('ag-a11y',v);sessionStorage.removeItem('ag-a11y');}
else{v=localStorage.getItem('ag-a11y');if(v!==null&&sessionStorage.getItem('ag-a11y')===null)sessionStorage.setItem('ag-a11y',v);localStorage.removeItem('ag-a11y');}}catch(e){}
try{if(m){s=m;if(K)localStorage.setItem('ag-a11y',JSON.stringify(m));else sessionStorage.setItem('ag-a11y',JSON.stringify(m));}else{s=JSON.parse((K?localStorage.getItem('ag-a11y'):sessionStorage.getItem('ag-a11y'))||'{}')||{};}}catch(e){s=m||{};}
try{var t={1:'ag-t125',2:'ag-t150'}[s.size];if(t)c.add(t);
var k={hc:'ag-hc',easy:'ag-easy',space:'ag-ls',ul:'ag-ul',motion:'ag-rm',saver:'ag-saver'};
for(var x in k){if(s[x])c.add(k[x]);}
var f=d.getAttribute('data-ag-easy-font');
if(s.easy&&f){var l=document.createElement('link');l.rel='stylesheet';l.id='ag-easy-font';l.href=f;document.head.appendChild(l);}
}catch(e){}})();
</script>
